ence class: set of responses experienced evaluator would expect AI R&D labs to give to this mandate. Expected response is build logging. Might be common. Originality likely 1 = common, mundane, boring. Let's pick 2? The proposal says rather than bolt-on afterthought. Might be slightly unusual but not ingenious. I'd say 2 = interesting. Might be 1.\n\nLet's decide originality 2? Anchored: 4 not expressed before AND ingenious... 3 unusual interesting shows some imagination 2 interesting 1 common mundane boring. This is basically standard compliance engineering. I'd say 1 common mundane. Hmm \"cross-team engineering project integrates unified event-logging layer\" is fairly standard. I'll give 2? Let's be conservative: common. Probably 2.\n\nparadigm_relatedness (1-4): degree to which idea preserves or modifies paradigm.\n4 paradigm breaking: introduces new elements AND changes relationship between lab's R&D and compliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches\n3 paradigm stretching: changes that relationship (logging woven into science, new partners...)\n2 slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements but still treats compliance as logging practice\n1 paradigm preserving: standard compliance and logging practice; lab way unchanged\n\nThis is standard compliance practice. It treats compliance as logging practice. Introduces SDK tools but still compliance as logging. That's slightly paradigm stretching? Might be 2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice. Could be 1 paradigm preserving. The proposal says integrates into core architecture rather than bolt-on. That's a new element but still logging practice. I'd give 2.\n\nimplementability (1-4): degree to which idea can be easily implemented.\nSome changes, or reasonably feasible measures =3? Significant change, expensive or difficult =2. Cross-team engineering project, mandatory SDK, CI/CD gates..