.\n2 = may have some benefit within special situation...\n1 = intervention not stated...\n\nIt directly applies: meet logging mandate. So 4.\n\neffectiveness (1-4):\n4 = reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability\n3 = reasonable and will contribute...\n2 = unreasonable...\n1 = solves unrelated...\n\nWill it solve? It records usage periods, reference databases, verification events as required. Article 12 also requires logging events relevant for risk etc., and automatic recording. Middleware seems reasonable. Might be partial? Probably will solve main problem. Score 4.\n\nimplementability (1-4):\n4 = easy to implement at low cost, or non-radical changes\n3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures\n2 = significant change, or expensive/difficult...\n1 = totally infeasible\n\nTwo-engineer squad three sprints reuse existing message-bus. That's reasonably feasible, some changes. Probably 3? Could be easy? \"some changes, or reasonably feasible measures\" = 3. Not low cost? Might be low cost. Hmm \"easy to implement at low cost, or non-radical changes\" =4. Reusing infrastructure, three sprints two engineers - maybe moderate. I'd say 3.\n\nacceptability (1-4):\n4 = common strategies that violate no norms\n3 = somewhat uncommon...\n2 = offends...\n1 = radically violates\n\nStandard compliance logging. Acceptable. 4.\n\nNeed output format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence sentence then <subscale> integer.\n\nProbably JSON? It says return rating echoing its id exactly. Provide lines.\n\nLet's produce structured output.\n\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: The middleware adds a tool/process but keeps compliance as separate logging practice without changing R&D-compliance relationship.\nparadigm_relatedness: 2\n\noriginality_evidence: Retrofitting standardized logging middleware into pipelines is a common, mundane compliance engineering response.\noriginality:1\n\napplicability_evidence: The proposal directly builds automatic event capture for usage periods, reference databases and verification events mandated by Article 12.\napplicability:4\n\neffectiveness_evidence: If implemented, the layer would provide the required logs for high-risk systems and convert per-project compliance cost into platform capability.\neffectiveness:4\n\nimplementability_evidence: Building the layer with two engineers over three sprints reusing existing message-bus infrastructure is reasonably feasible but requires dedicated squad time and process change.\nimplementability:3\n\nacceptability_evidence: Standardized logging middleware for regulatory traceability is a common, norm-compliant strategy that does not offend legal or business sensibilities.\nacceptability:4\n\nReturn.\n\n",
