uld offend sensibilities somewhat? Might be somewhat uncommon or unusual strategies that do not offend sensibilities =3. Or offends sensibilities somewhat? Sharing logs even anonymized might be legally risky. Possibly 2? Acceptability anchor: 4 common strategies violate no norms; 3 somewhat uncommon or unusual strategies that do not offend sensibilities; 2 offends sensibilities somewhat but is not totally unacceptable; 1 radically violates laws.\n\nRepurposing mandatory logs for research with academic partners and open benchmark. Could be acceptable if anonymized, but high-risk systems logging may contain personal data. Might be legally sensitive. I'd say somewhat uncommon but does not offend sensibilities -> 3. Maybe 2? Hmm.\n\nGiven regulatory text requires logs include identification of natural persons involved in verification etc., and input data for which search led to match. Sharing that externally is likely prohibited. So acceptability maybe low. Could be offends sensibilities somewhat. Might be 2.\n\nLet's pick acceptability =3? The proposal says anonymised log streams. That mitigates. Could still be acceptable. I'd give 3.\n\nWe need output format: echo id exactly. For each subscale in order list <subscale>_evidence then <subscale>.\n\nProbably JSON.\n\nLet's produce:\n\nP2252\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: ...\nparadigm_relatedness:3\n...\n\nEnsure one sentence evidence.\n\nProvide concise.\n\n",
