eresting shows some imagination. 2 = interesting. 1 = common mundane boring.\n\nRetrofit middleware is common. Probably 1 = common, mundane, boring. Or maybe 2 interesting? Likely common compliance approach. I'd say 1 common mundane.\n\nimplementability: 4 easy low cost non-radical changes. 3 some changes reasonably feasible. 2 significant change expensive/difficult but not impossible. 1 totally infeasible.\n\nFour-engineer team two sprints per system wrap interfaces writing to existing time-series DB. Seems reasonably feasible, some changes. Could be 3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures. Or 4 easy? Might need engineering effort. Probably 3.\n\nacceptability: 4 common strategies violate no norms. 3 somewhat uncommon does not offend. 2 offends somewhat. 1 radically violates...\n\nLogging middleware is acceptable legally. 4 = common strategies that violate no norms.\n\napplicability: 4 solves identified problem directly related to stated problem (do X to get Y, and Y is part of stated problem). Problem is decide how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D. This proposal does X to get logging compliance. Yes directly related. So 4.\n\neffectiveness: 4 reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability. Will it solve? It targets specific data points Article12(3) mandates for Annex III category1(a). Might meet mandate. Reasonable will solve main problem of meeting logging mandate. Could be 4.\n\nIf you could do it, would solve main problem. Yes.\n\nThus scores:\nparadigm_relatedness 2\noriginality 1\nimplementability 3\nacceptability 4\napplicability 4\neffectiveness 4\n\nNeed format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence sentence then <subscale> integer.\n\nProbably output JSON or lines.\n\nLet's produce:\n\nid: P2332\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: ...\nparadigm_relatedness: 2\n...\n\nMake sure one sentence evidence.\n\nProvide concise.\n\n",
