ow cost, or non-radical changes -> adding template and quarterly review. Some changes reasonably feasible. Could be 3 some changes, or reasonably feasible measures. Or 4 easy low cost. Adding two-page template and chairing reviews is low cost. Probably 4 easy to implement at low cost, or non-radical changes. I'd say 4.\n\nApplicability: solves identified problem directly related to stated problem (do X to get Y, and Y is part of stated problem). Stated problem: decide how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D accordingly. Approval means committing scarce implementation resources. Proposal addresses cost estimation before greenlight to avoid overruns. Directly applies to meeting logging mandate with resource commitment. So 4.\n\nEffectiveness: reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability? It will help manage costs but does it ensure logging compliance? It gates projects based on cost, may defer. Does it solve logging mandate? It prevents budget overruns but doesn't guarantee logs are technically compliant. It contributes to solution. Probably 3 = reasonable and will contribute to solution of problem (it helps, but only partial). Could be 4? It solves resource allocation problem but not technical logging. I think partial: 3.\n\nReturn JSON? Instruction says give <subscale>_evidence then <subscale>. Echo id exactly. Provide rating.\n\nProbably output lines.\n\nLet's produce:\n\nid P1655\noriginality_evidence: ...\noriginality 3\netc.\n\nEnsure one sentence evidence.\n\nProceed.",
