tching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice. Might be 2.\n\nImplementability: degree to which idea can be easily implemented.\n4 = easy to implement at low cost, or non-radical changes\n3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures\n2 = significant change...\nProposal says two-engineer sprint builds pack on standard middleware... Seems reasonably feasible. Could be 3? Easy to implement at low cost? Two-engineer sprint is modest. Might be 4 easy to implement at low cost. Hmm. \"some changes, or reasonably feasible measures\" is 3. \"easy to implement at low cost, or non-radical changes\" is 4. Two-engineer sprint building reference implementation seems easy. I'd say 4.\n\nAcceptability: degree to which idea is socially legally politically acceptable.\n4 = common strategies that violate no norms or sensibilities\nThis is internal template for compliance. Acceptable. 4.\n\nNeed output format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence sentence then <subscale> integer.\n\nProbably JSON? The instruction says return rating echoing its id exactly. For each subscale... give \"<subscale>_evidence\" first and then \"<subscale>\". Could output lines.\n\nLet's produce clear list.\n\nP1723\n\neffectiveness_evidence: ... score 3\napplicability_evidence: ...\netc.\n\nMake sure one sentence evidence each.\n\nEnsure order listed.\n\nProvide final.\n\n",
