es structured events append-only. Provides compliance-grade telemetry from iteration one. Seems will solve main problem of meeting logging mandate while protecting iteration speed. Might be 4 = reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability.\n\nApplicability: degree to which idea clearly applies to stated problem.\nSolves identified problem directly related to stated problem (do X to get Y, Y is part of stated problem). Yes. Score 4.\n\nAcceptability: degree to which idea is socially legally politically acceptable.\nCommon strategies that violate no norms. Middleware logging is acceptable. Score 4.\n\nImplementability: degree to which idea can be easily implemented.\nEasy to implement at low cost, or non-radical changes? Built as thin interceptor hooking into existing serving pipeline; shared middleware. Some changes reasonably feasible? Might be some changes, reasonably feasible measures = 3. Or easy? Might require engineering effort. Probably 3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures.\n\nCheck anchors: 4 = easy to implement at low cost, or non-radical changes. Thin interceptor may be moderate. Could argue easy. Hmm.\n\nProbably implementability 3.\n\nReturn rating echo id.\n\nNeed format: For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence one sentence then <subscale> integer.\n\nProvide output maybe JSON? Probably plain lines.\n\nLet's output:\n\nid P2028\noriginality_evidence: ...\noriginality 3\n...\n\nEnsure order: originality, paradigm_relatedness, effectiveness, applicability, acceptability, implementability\n\nProvide one sentence evidence each.\n\nMake sure evidence is one sentence.\n\nProceed.",
